{
  "schema": "lean-proof-simplification-evidence-v1",
  "source_commit": "a37047cc30ac083a7ea4fd20743ab676a9a3e293",
  "source_parent": "06b57b8fa2931b795d13ca783f3a2759b42f1454",
  "scope": "Simplify ArithmeticPow perturbation-coefficient polynomial identity",
  "validation": "Paired target and four tracked Lean direct clients pass; Sandwich and ControllerLift objects match. TilingWord and BinomExpansion object bytes differ, but their names/types/axioms and global simp/instance reports match with target and client objects pinned. Direct project provider source/object pairs match prior current-source producer receipts.",
  "limitations": [
    "Other project, Foundation and Mathlib transitive dependencies remain cached; direct provider source hashes come from earlier producer receipts rather than fresh source samples during these builds.",
    "Initial baseline Sandwich used source-current but older PowerRecovery 5f4cdf45… and is superseded by the current-Congruences provider replay; its original input symlink was repointed, while the receipt preserves the resolved old provider hash. Initial TilingWord failed on missing TilingRows and the saved receipt/log/time show the setup failure.",
    "Both failed standalone proof probes are retained, while the successful standalone probe lacks full input pins. The selected paired builds provide validation.",
    "Single shared-load timing pairs do not establish general performance changes. Matching declarations and registrations do not establish equality of proof bodies, every persistent extension or untested downstream behavior.",
    "Compiled objects, including the saved superseded Sandwich object, are excluded; recorded hashes and paths require external objects for independent byte verification.",
    "B separately used the candidate Pow and candidate-Pow-built BinomExpansion objects in a four-wrapper replay; that separate evidence is not part of this bundle."
  ],
